{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1549858-contracts-and-favored-regalia","id":1549858,"title":"Contracts and Favored Regalia","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-04-05T19:29:09-07:00","id":1549858,"title":"Contracts and Favored Regalia","content":"I have a question regarding Contracts and favored Regalia. Now the way I understand it is this. At character creation a player starts off with the favored Regalia of what ever Seeming they happen to be like say Sword for an Elemental and the player then chooses a Second favored regalia lets say Jewels as well. Now, I am under the impression that when choosing Contracts a player has to choose at least two contracts from Favored Regalia, which I took to mean the initial favored regalia based on Seeming while the remaining contracts are chosen from among the secondary favored regalia, court, and goblin Contracts. Now my question is this, am I wrong in this assumption and could a player purchase contracts form Crown, Mirror, Shield, and Steed as the player has at least two contracts from his two favored regalia of Sword and Jewels?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24961-darklander","name":"Darklander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-05T21:26:01-07:00","id":1549861,"title":"","content":"You're incorrect. The required contracts from favored regalia can be from either favored regalia.<br /> <br /> Let's say you're an Ogre, favoring the Shield. You choose also to favor the Sword, so your favored regalia are Sword and Shield.<br /> You get four Common Contracts. Two of these must be from your favored regalia, so either two Common Sword, two Common Shield, or a Common Sword and a Common Shield. The other two Common Contracts can be of any regalia, any court (providing you qualify), or can be goblin contracts. So they can include a Common Steed, or a Common Summer, or a Common goblin contract, or whatever.<br /> Then you get two Royal Contracts. Each Royal must be from a favored regalia or your court (providing you qualify). So you can have a Royal Sword and a Royal Shield, or if you have Mantle (Spring) 3 you could have a Royal Sword and a Royal Spring, or various combinations. But you can't start with a Royal Steed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-06T06:04:42-07:00","id":1549868,"title":"","content":"So if I am understanding you correctly, If I had an Elemental/Delver of the Winter Court that has Sword and Jewels as favored Regalia, the first two common contracts would have to be two common/Sword, two common/Jewels or one of each, but the second two can be any of the 6 common regalia, Winter court or goblin contracts. While the two Royals can only be Favored Regalia or Winter Court","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24961-darklander","name":"Darklander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-06T07:57:52-07:00","id":1549870,"title":"","content":"Mostly correct. The second two commons can actually include non-Winter court contracts too, provided you are qualified to purchase them as per the rules on p. 150 - meaning, to buy more than one common contract from an outside court, you need Court Goodwill 2 with them.<br /> <br /> When the game refers to &quot;Common Regalia Contracts,&quot; that's not designating regalia as common or uncommon. It means regalia contracts - so not court or goblin - that are common contracts - the less expensive, roughly less powerful ones. There isn't a category of &quot;common regalia.&quot; So if you have the Kith &amp; Kin book that introduces new regalia, your second two common contracts can include contracts from those regalia outside the corebook 6, too. They can just be common contracts from any regalia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 04-06-2025, 11:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-06T08:28:17-07:00","id":1549871,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the clarification I really appreciated it. So given your further clarification my Elemental/Delver of the Winter Court who has Sword and Jewels as Favored Regalia could purchase 2 common contracts from Sword, Jewels or one of each, then 2 common Contracts from any of the six regalia, Goblin, or Court contracts including outside court contracts provided I chose the appropriate court goodwill merit as well. While the 2 Royal Contracts can only be from Favored Regalia and Winter Court.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24961,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24961-darklander","user":"Darklander","date":". 04-06-2025, 11:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24961-darklander","name":"Darklander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-06T08:38:02-07:00","id":1549872,"title":"","content":"That's correct!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-06T08:44:17-07:00","id":1549873,"title":"","content":"Again Thank you very much for your assistance","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24961-darklander","name":"Darklander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}